From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: let the seek helper own recovery resets

A3.20: integrated after GE-Proton11-6 and the project seek/error patches.
Historical A3.19 inputs and installed artifacts remain unchanged.

The inherited OnVideoStreamTick recovery branches clear the frame sink
before calling media_engine_set_current_time(). That helper first checks
MFSESSIONCAP_SEEK and returns without seeking when the capability is absent
or its query fails. The preceding reset has already dropped queued and
presentation samples and cleared sample_request_pending, without submitting
replacement demand. A refused recovery can therefore damage a live source.

Remove only the redundant caller resets. The helper already resets after
checking capability and before an accepted seek/paused seek. Its intentional
early returns (including logical end and coalesced seek) now keep their own
semantics. No retry, new recovery condition, threshold, error suppression,
GetSeekable compatibility change, or queue-size change is introduced.

Neither recovery warning appeared in the captured A3.19 session, so this is
a source-level preventive correction, NOT an explanation of the observed
episode #331 seek stalls or WaterWolf quality. Python model tests are not
Wine runtime or playback validation.

The license of the modified Wine source file applies to this patch.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -4277,7 +4277,6 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_OnVideoStreamTick(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface, LONGLONG *pts)
             {
                 WARN("Video sample %.6f is too far ahead of clock %.6f; resynchronizing.\n",
                         mftime_to_seconds(*pts), mftime_to_seconds(clocktime));
-                video_frame_sink_reset(engine->presentation.frame_sink);
                 media_engine_set_current_time(engine, mftime_to_seconds(clocktime));
                 *pts = MINLONGLONG;
             }
@@ -4296,7 +4295,6 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_OnVideoStreamTick(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface, LONGLONG *pts)
                         WARN("Presentation clock stalled at %.6f; restarting stream.\n",
                                 mftime_to_seconds(clocktime));
                         engine->stalled_clock_seek_time = now;
-                        video_frame_sink_reset(engine->presentation.frame_sink);
                         media_engine_set_current_time(engine, mftime_to_seconds(clocktime));
                         *pts = MINLONGLONG;
                     }
